Consistently ranked among the top ten “Best Firms to Work For” and Engineering News-Record’s top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.
Job Summary
Langan is seeking a
Geospatial
Systems Engineer
to join its national Digital Solutions Team. This individual will play a crucial role in designing and implementing systems that support both current and future Enterprise GIS environments. In this role, you will have the opportunity to be part of a growing and fast-paced technology team that works on Esri ArcGIS Enterprise deployments across on-premises, Azure, and AWS cloud environments for both internal and customer projects.
Job Responsibilities
Collaborate with Langan’s geospatial, network and development teams to design and build ArcGIS Enterprise environments that serve both internal and external clients;
Perform ArcGIS Enterprise installation, configuration, maintenance and support;
Apply concepts of computing, networking, security, and the cloud to system design;
Understand and apply Esri licensing and server roles;
Troubleshoot and debug issues in existing server environments;
Plan, develop, test, and document disaster recovery, redundancy, and backup activities for Enterprise GIS environments;
Develop and maintain scripts to automate application installation, configuration, and administration;
Write comprehensive documentation on system implementations and changes;
Manage and apply updates to services and systems;
Assist with third party integrations as per project requirements;
Stay up to date with emerging trends and technologies, cloud & systems engineering; and
Respond to incidents by helping with recovery, mitigation, and root cause analysis.
Qualifications
Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Systems Engineering, or other related discipline is required (Master’s degree a plus);
2 + years of real-world experience designing, executing, and supporting Esri ArcGIS Enterprise;
Experience identifying and resolving complex technical issues;
Self-motivated learner who continually keeps up to date with new technology;
Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;
High caliber of self-motivation with the ability to work well within groups;
Ability to work efficiently and produce accurate and thorough work;
Ability to work independently, remain flexible, and handle multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment;
Experience with Esri’s ArcGIS Enterprise 11.x;
Experience in planning and deploying cloud solutions on either Azure or AWS;
Ability to troubleshoot Windows Server 2016+;
Understanding of basic networking concepts: IP, DNS, firewall rules, vNets/VPCs, etc;
Understand the key capabilities of Esri ArcGIS solutions, applications, and APIs;
Differentiate between ArcGIS Enterprise deployment patterns;
Familiarity with Shell/CLIs such as Bash or PowerShell;
Experience working with security concepts such as Role-Based Access Control, SSL, authentication and authorization, etc; and
Proactive and comprehensive troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.
